       }
      ],
      "text": "Metoclopramide:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for symptomatic, documented GERD in adults who fail conventional therapy, 10 to 15 mg PO 30 minutes before each meal and at bedtime (max 60 mg/day) for 4 to 12 weeks; 12 weeks is the maximum duration."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Contraindicated with a history of tardive dyskinesia."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Avoid other drugs that cause TD, EPS or NMS (eg, antipsychotics), and avoid use in Parkinson disease; it may raise BP, so avoid in hypertension or with MAOIs."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
